# The `_ipp` stack is what makes this tenant printable: while it is active,
# every printer registered with txco://ipp/printer answers at
# `ipps://ipp.<zone>/p/<label>`, and every job printed to one arrives here — AFTER the client was
# told the job completed. The chassis's work ended when this run started;
# what happens to the document from here on is this rule's business.
#
# Facts ride under @ipp.* (all read-only): printer, job_id, job_number,
# job_name, requesting_user (client-claimed — untrusted), submitted_at, and
# document{sha256, size, format, name}. There are NO bytes in the envelope:
# the document is already in the tenant's blob store, addressed by sha256.
# There is no @ipp.copies either — this printer has no paper.
#
# WHO printed is @principal.id (with .kind and .credential): the principal
# the printer is granted to, pinned by the chassis after it signed in. A
# stack that serves several people gates on it here.
#
# @ipp.printer is the label after /p/ in the printer URL — a registered
# printer's. What the label MEANS is this stack's decision. Here every printer files its documents under its
# own name — print to /p/research and the page lands in research/<job id>.
# `from_sha` adopts the already-stored object; nothing is copied.
WHEN @src == "ipp"
  EXEC "txco://blob/put"
    WITH name = &concat(@ipp.printer, "/", @ipp.job_id),
         from_sha = @ipp.document.sha256,
         content_type = @ipp.document.format,
         filename = @ipp.job_name,
         into = "_kept"
